# What must not reach a build context.
#
# The first reason is correctness, not size. `dotnet restore` runs in the image and writes its
# answer to obj/project.assets.json; a later COPY of the same folder from a Windows machine puts
# that machine's assets file on top of it, and the publish then looks for packages that were never
# restored here. That failure reads as "Package System.Text.Json, version 6.0.10 was not found",
# which says nothing about the real cause.
#
# The second reason is that a build context carries whatever it is given: a .venv, a node_modules,
# a browser profile and an env file are all things that have no business inside an image.

# Build output. See above: these actively break the build, they do not merely bloat it.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/dist/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
.build/

# Secrets. Nothing in an image, and nothing in a layer that an image is made from.
**/*.env
!deploy/.env.example
api.env
api_key.env

# Local state and captures, regenerated and never source.
diagnostics/
**/diagnostics/
**/*.log
**/*.jsonl
_local-before-branch-restore/
**/_local-before-branch-restore/

# Nothing in these is needed to build the backend, the dashboard or the worker. The Windows-only
# projects are left out one by one rather than by a blanket rule, because the worker genuinely does
# build from Windows/src - just not from these.
Windows/src/ZoomAutoAdmit.WindowsUI/
Windows/src/ZoomAutoAdmit.WindowsRuntime/
Windows/src/ZoomAutoAdmit.UIAutomation/**
# Its project file is read by restore (Attendance names it for its Windows target); nothing else is.
!Windows/src/ZoomAutoAdmit.UIAutomation/ZoomAutoAdmit.UIAutomation.csproj
Windows/src/ZoomAutoAdmit.Inspector/
Windows/src/ZoomAutoAdmit.WaitingRoomAutomation/
Windows/src/ZoomAutoAdmit.WaitingRoomTester/
Windows/src/ZoomAutoAdmit.Setup/
# The cloud worker uses the cross-platform session-role library.
Windows/tests/*
!Windows/tests/ZoomAutoAdmit.WebAutomation.Tests/
!Windows/tests/ZoomAutoAdmit.WebAutomation.Tests/**
Windows/design-reference/
Windows/installer/
Windows/web/

# The macOS half.
Sources/
Tests/
AppBundle/
Package.swift

# Repository furniture.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
**/*.md
!Backend/README.md
